Package: spaRkbricks
Title: Connect to Databricks Spark with Multi-Auth Support (OAuth and PAT)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Marck", "Vaisman", email = "marck@synaptiq.ai", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides functions to connect to Databricks Spark clusters using
    either OAuth (via Databricks CLI) or Personal Access Token (PAT) authentication.
    Uses the sparkbricks Python package via reticulate for reliable connectivity,
    automatic OAuth token refresh, and proper session management. Includes cluster
    lifecycle management (start/stop) and properly handles session cleanup.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.2.3
URL: https://github.com/mvaisman/spaRkbricks
BugReports: https://github.com/mvaisman/spaRkbricks/issues
Imports:
    reticulate (>= 1.35),
    sparklyr (>= 1.8.0)
Suggests:
    dplyr,
    dbplyr,
    here,
    dotenv
Config/reticulate:
  list(
    packages = list(
      list(package = "sparkbricks", pip = TRUE)
    )
  )
